description:
FOUND s508a (Opus 5.5, 2026-10-05) while probing #2645; PRE-EXISTING on main fee16466 (base extraction answers the same).

REPRODUCER (perl 5.40.3 vs PCL):
  our $x = "G";
  my $x = "X";
  sub f2 { "$x-" . $x }
  print f2(), "\n";
perl: X-X      PCL: G-G   (silent)

The capture promotion runs (PCL_SPAN_DEBUG: `CAPPROMOTE $x -> $x__file__0`, and the p-sub's `:captures` lists `$x__file__0`), but the sub BODY still reads `$x` -- the package variable -- so the rename did not reach the body: the in-scope `our $x` is resolved first.  perl's rule: a later `my $x` in the same scope MASKS the earlier `our $x` (perl warns `"my" variable $x masks earlier declaration in same scope` only under -w for my/my; our-then-my is silent).  Probe: scratch/s508a/probes/k33.pl (s508a worktree).
Cheap discriminating measurement (not taken): PCL_SPAN_DEBUG + dump the sub body's tokens after _rewrite_var_uses -- if the Symbol was rewritten and the emission still says `$x`, the our-alias resolver re-maps it at lowering; if it was not rewritten, `$skip` (_ref_shadowed) treats the file `our` as a shadow.
